### 7.1 Introduction

The preceding chapters established a rigorous theoretical framework for Energy–Information Unified Networks (EIUN), proving exponential stability (Theorem 4.1), Wasserstein consensus convergence (Theorem 5.1), and a fundamental thermodynamic efficiency bound (Theorem 6.2). To fully substantiate these claims, systematic numerical validation is essential. Due to the interdisciplinary nature of the work—requiring co‑simulation of power systems, wireless channels, and distributed optimisation—the development of the complete simulation environment has been a significant undertaking. At the time of writing, the modular simulation software described in Appendix K has been implemented and verified on elementary test cases, but the comprehensive experimental campaign originally envisioned could not be completed within the thesis timeline.

