**Appendix H**  
**Spectral Properties of the Power‑Aware Laplacian**

We collect useful bounds for the eigenvalues of \(\mathbf{L}(\boldsymbol{\sigma})\).

**Lemma H.1.** If the underlying graph with edge set \(\mathcal{E}_{\text{active}}\) is connected and each active edge satisfies \(w_{ij} \ge w_{\min} > 0\), then

\[
\lambda_2(\mathbf{L}) \ge w_{\min} \lambda_2(\mathbf{L}_0),
\]

where \(\mathbf{L}_0\) is the Laplacian of the unweighted graph (all edges have weight 1).

*Proof.* For any vector \(\mathbf{v} \perp \mathbf{1}\),

\[
\mathbf{v}^\top \mathbf{L} \mathbf{v} = \sum_{(i,j)} w_{ij} (v_i - v_j)^2 \ge w_{\min} \sum_{(i,j)} (v_i - v_j)^2 = w_{\min} \mathbf{v}^\top \mathbf{L}_0 \mathbf{v}.
\]

The result follows from the Rayleigh quotient. ∎

**Lemma H.2 (Persistent connectivity via time averaging).** If the time‑varying Laplacian \(\mathbf{L}(t)\) satisfies \(\frac{1}{T_r}\int_t^{t+T_r} \lambda_2(\mathbf{L}(s))\,ds \ge \nu > 0\) for all \(t\), then the system is exponentially stable with rate proportional to \(\nu\) (see Theorem 4.1 and the discussion in Chapter 4).

